  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Text printed primarily on coarse brown paper illustrated with mimeographed border designs. Collage mounted at top and laced with brown ribbon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Cover of book made of wrinkled brown paper, with title and author printed in black on white paper, cut out, hand-painted, and collaged on to front cover. Below, roll of cardboard paper is attached, and tied with fabric, resembling a scroll. Blue paper label on roll says "Sacerdotisa Lissette" in black lettering. Back cover has large hand-painted cut-out of female head with Vigía lamp sprouting from her crown, surrounded by leaves and designs, the publisher and series appearing in a circle around the lamp. Decorative fixed and loose endpapers how female face appearing among leaves.Collaging and hand-coloring appears on preliminary sheets. Most text printed on coarse brown paper with decorative borders.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Consta de doscientos ejemplares ... En su confección fueron usados papeles de diferentes texturas y gramajes."--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
